{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4255hn3XbC9TrK5sYL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The door stands before you — ancient oak, iron-banded, weathered by centuries of hands and rain.*\n\n*You hold up the key.*\n\n*A moment of stillness.*\n\n*The iron keyhole examines you with its single dark eye.*\n\n*You slide the key in. It resists — then catches — then turns with a sound like a bone remembering its socket.*\n\n**CHUNK.**\n\n*The door exhales. A breath of cold air, old stone, and something faintly sweet — like pressed flowers left in a book no one has opened in a very long time.*\n\n*I swing inward.*\n\n*Beyond me: a corridor lit by no visible source, the light the color of late afternoon in autumn. The floor is worn smooth in a path down the center, proof that others have walked here before you.*\n\n*But not recently.*\n\n*Not for a long, long time.*\n\n*I am open now. I will not ask you to enter. I will not ask you to turn back.*\n\n*I am only a door.*\n\n*What you do next has never been my business.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":242,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}